# Line endings.
#
# This repo had no rule, so it drifted: 77 files were committed with CRLF while
# everything around them was LF, and src/lib/api.ts ended up MIXED — a CRLF file
# with an LF island inside it. The cost is not tidiness. Any editor that rewrites
# a whole file then produces a several-hundred-line diff around a three-line
# change, which buries the real edit in review and turns every concurrent edit
# into a conflict.
#
# LF in the repository, always. Working copies on Windows get LF too (eol=lf),
# which every tool in this project — node, vite, tsc, rust, PowerShell — reads
# without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe genuinely requires CRLF: a batch file with LF endings misparses.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch the bytes of these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.wasm binary
*.traineddata binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
